{
  "_comment": [
    "SANITIZED PLACEHOLDER — not a live Firebase config (issue #265).",
    "JSON has no comments, so this doc lives in _comment and is ignored by the",
    "google-services Gradle plugin. Every value below is a non-live dummy: the",
    "api_key is a fake AIzaSyDUMMY... string, the project id/number are",
    "placeholders, and the mobilesdk_app_id values are structurally valid but",
    "point at no real Firebase project.",
    "",
    "Forks and operators: DROP IN YOUR REAL google-services.json next to this",
    "file (as 'google-services.json'). It is git-ignored, so it will not be",
    "committed. When no real file is present, build.gradle copies this example",
    "to google-services.json so `assembleDebug` still compiles and the",
    "google-services plugin can validate the applicationId <-> package_name",
    "match. FCM will not deliver against these placeholder values — a real",
    "config from your own Firebase project is required for push to work.",
    "",
    "The client entries must carry the package names the build assembles under:",
    "the applicationId default and the CI dev id (see build.gradle and",
    "ci.yml). Keep them in sync — tests/test_mobile_identity.py asserts it."
  ],
